# coaching-service — do not fill this in by hand.
#
# Every value this service needs is generated from the repository root:
#
#     cp .env.example .env      # once, at the repo root
#     npm run setup:env         # generates services/*/.env for all 15
#     npm run check:env         # verifies they are present and current
#
# PORT and peer service URLs are derived from the port table in
# scripts/run-all.sh, so they cannot drift from what actually runs.
#
# Do NOT set DIRECT_DATABASE_URL. Nothing at runtime reads it; the migration
# scripts derive it (session port 5432 plus this service's ?schema= pin).
# Use `npm run migrate:all` and `npm run migrate:status`.
#
# Pooler flags (pgbouncer, connection_limit, pool_timeout) are applied once, by
# this service's PrismaService, from DB_CONNECTION_LIMIT in the root .env.
#
# A value this service alone must differ on goes in services/coaching-service/.env.override
# (git-ignored, merged at generation time). Security-relevant keys are rejected
# there: NODE_ENV, INTERNAL_SECRET, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY,
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL.
